; The compiler on the BBC Model B+128 at its full capacities (SMALL 0). This is the developer's
; form, `*RUN LATHEC ARGS`, its banks in the module's RAM form (slot 4), loaded by the start-up
; code; bbcrom.rom_env makes the ROM form's environment from it: banks 1 to 5 of the module's
; image, read only, the window $8050-$BFDF, started by `*LATHE ARGS` (the same objects). The
; same image in the RAM form, filled by `*RUN LOADMOD`, is the third form.
; lathe/tests/test_bbc_selfhost.py builds all three; lathe/docs/bbc.md, "Step 4, as built", has
; the layout and the measurements.
;
; Fixed in main RAM: the run-time modules (bbc, rt_bbc, rt_math, rt_frame), sys, and the
; functions the linker keeps fixed because they have a `with` block or run inside one (kernel's,
; fbuf's, lex's, decl's, out's, err's and src's: 7,974 bytes on 2026-11-17). Everything else is
; placed, by the far calls between the modules (lathe/tests/farcall_matrix.py): bank 1 expr,
; parts and out (15,466 bytes as the linker judges it, before zero page shrinks the code, of
; 16,272 in the ROM form; out is in bank 4 in the developer's form, where a bank holds its
; variables too, 16,352 bytes); bank 2 gen and lathec; bank 3 decl and asmblock; bank 4
; inlines, kernel, lex, fbuf, src and err; bank 5 reg, cond, fold and typetab. In the ROM form
; the variables of the placed modules are in main RAM too.
;
; The split: in the ROM form at $4F00, about halfway between the end of the code ($47A9 with
; BBCFS 1; $4756 since the texts of the errors went to the message file, below) and where the
; variables need to start (2026-11-17, after kernel's sym_find, thaw and freeze left fixed
; memory; $5020 before, $5000 on 2026-11-15). The developer's form has its
; own, $57A0 (code to $4989 with BBCFS 1; $5200 before), as bbcfs is fixed there: its
; start-up loads the banks through bbc.open, which with BBCFS 1 calls bbcfs.map, and a bank is
; not there before it is loaded. In the ROM form the banks are always there, so bbcfs is in
; bank 5. The `when ROMFORM` entries are the ROM form's and the `unless ROMFORM` entries the
; developer's: bbcrom.rom_env defines ROMFORM as 1 (lathe/docs/configurations.md, "The
; environment file").
;
; With `define ADFS 1` main RAM starts at $1F00, ADFS's PAGE with the DFS beside it, for a
; machine with ADFS (and BBCFS 2, ADFS's names): the `when ADFS` entries. The splits are $5220
; in the ROM form and $5B00 in the developer's, halfway again (code to $4DD8 and $501B with
; BBCFS 2, 2026-11-17; the ROM form's to $4D85 with the message file); $5640 and $58A0 before that, $5600 and $5880 until rt_frame's list
; routines (measured 2026-11-17 with BBCFS 2, before them: the code ended
; at $55E5 and $5828, the ROM form's variables filled $5600-$7BFF and $0401-$06B1, 104 bytes
; free in all; lathe/docs/bbc.md, "ADFS"). BBCFS 2 with ADFS 0 fits the developer's form
; since then (it was 132 bytes over its split).
;
; Regions, in the four sideways RAM slots: kernel's name heap in slot 12; err's messages
; (constants: loaded at start-up in the developer's form; the ROM form has none, its texts are
; written by the module image: `when ROMFORM define TEXTS_IN_MODULE 1`, lathe/docs/bbc.md,
; "The texts in the module"), fbuf's buffer and labels, lex's string and kernel's saved tokens in slot
; 13; the symbol table in slot 0; OUT's table and DECL's import rows in slot 1.
;
; The 128 KB module (eight banks: lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The 128 KB module"): bbcrom.rom_env with
; eight banks defines ROM128 as 1, and the banks are the image's 0 to 4. The layout is the same
; as in the sixteen-bank image (above; it was the eight-bank image's own until 2026-11-17, when
; parts and out moved to expr's bank and the sixteen-bank image took it too): the self-compile
; makes 529,452 far calls so (counted), against 728,822 in the sixteen-bank image's layout
; before; as judged the banks are 15,466, 15,396, 15,343, 12,342 and 13,648 bytes of 16,272
; (2026-11-17, with the message file; 14,273 the fifth with BBCFS 2, whose bbcfs is there).
;
; The 32K Model B (RAM32 1: bbcrom.rom_env(..., settings={'RAM32': 1}); lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The 32K
; Model B"): no sideways RAM, so every region is fixed in main RAM, and FIXED_REGIONS tells the
; compiler so (-fNAME), so that no function stays fixed for a `with` block; SMALL 1 with the twins'
; `#if RAM32` capacities; the ROM form with ADFS 0 only. Five banks of 14,239 to 15,829 bytes as
; judged (15,476 to 16,071 before a token's place became one record, 15,667 to 16,170 before FBUF
; left out the stores nothing reads), fold fixed; 178 bytes of main RAM free (BBCFS 1,
; 2026-11-18). The 32K image is the module's eight-bank form, the texts of the errors in two
; parts (lathe/tests/test_bbc_ram32.py).
; Image B, the image for machines with no sideways RAM (RAM32 1 with ADAPT 1: lathe/docs/bbc.md,
; "The image for machines with no sideways RAM"): the 32K Model B's form with BBCFS 3 and its own
; capacities (the twins' `#if ADAPT` inside `#if RAM32`), kernel.names lowest in main RAM from the
; DFS's PAGE (`region NAMES fixed $1900`: 4,646 bytes, $1900-$2B25), the code above it ($2B26, 5,334
; bytes resident) and the variables from its end; 6 bytes of main RAM free (2026-11-21). As it starts
; the compiler begins the heap at PAGE when PAGE is higher (kernel.init, OSBYTE 131), so with ADFS
; ($1F00) it has 3,110 bytes; the module refuses *LATHE at a PAGE above $1F00 (HIGHEST_PAGE).
cpu       6502
zeropage  $00 $8F
define    ROMFORM 0     ; the developer's form; bbcrom.rom_env makes it 1, the ROM form
define    ADFS 0        ; 1: PAGE is ADFS's with the DFS beside it, $1F00 (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "ADFS")
define    RAM32 0       ; 1: the 32K Model B, every table in main RAM (below; the ROM form, ADFS 0)
define    ADAPT 0       ; 1: the image for every machine with sideways RAM (below; the ROM form, ADFS 1)
unless    RAM32 unless ADFS unless ROMFORM code $1900 $579F  ; bbcfs is fixed in the developer's form (below)
unless    RAM32 unless ADFS unless ROMFORM data $57A0 $7BFF
unless    RAM32 unless ADFS when ROMFORM code $1900 $4EFF
unless    RAM32 unless ADFS when ROMFORM data $4F00 $7BFF
unless    RAM32 when ADFS unless ROMFORM code $1F00 $5AFF   ; at ADFS's PAGE
unless    RAM32 when ADFS unless ROMFORM data $5B00 $7BFF
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT when ADFS when ROMFORM code $1F00 $521F
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT when ADFS when ROMFORM data $5220 $7BFF
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT code $1F00 $523F  ; the image for every machine with sideways RAM: its list (below)
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT data $5240 $7BFF  ; after the code, which is free once rt_place has read it
when      RAM32 unless ADAPT code $1900 $2E2F
when      RAM32 unless ADAPT data $2E30 $7BFF
when      RAM32 when ADAPT code $2B26 $3FFB  ; Image B: kernel.names from $1900, below the code (below)
when      RAM32 when ADAPT data $3FFC $7BFF
more      data $0401 $06FF
exit      return $0400  ; the start-up code keeps S at $0400 (bbc.KEEP), and ends with RTS
output    raw
define    BOARD 3       ; the BBC (lathe/host/driver/boards.py)
define    PORTS 2       ; lathe/src/sys.lth over lathe/rt/bbc.lth
define    BBCFS 0       ; file names as given; 1 the DFS's, 2 ADFS's, 3 those of the one OSARGS names (lathe/rt/bbc/bbcfs.lth)
unless    ROMFORM define TEXTS_IN_MODULE 0  ; the texts of the errors in the tool
when      ROMFORM define TEXTS_IN_MODULE 1  ; the ROM form's, in the module (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The texts in the module")
define    MODULE_SLOT 4 ; the module's slot: rt_bbc.SLOT, and the emulator's --bbc-module-slot
unless    RAM32 define SMALL 0  ; the tables at full size
when      RAM32 define SMALL 1    ; the 32K Model B's capacities: RAM32 within SMALL in the twins
when      RAM32 define FIXED_REGIONS 1  ; -fNAME for each region below: their blocks map nothing
unless    ADAPT define ROOMS 0  ; the tables' capacities fixed by the build
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT define ROOMS 1  ; set as the tool starts: the placer writes them
                                  ; (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "Capacities set at start-up")
when      RAM32 when ADAPT define ROOMS 0  ; Image B: fixed by the build, the name heap begun at PAGE
when      RAM32 when ADAPT define HIGHEST_PAGE $1F00  ; Image B: the module refuses *LATHE above it
define    ROM128 0      ; bbcrom.rom_env makes it 1 for the eight-bank image (above)
window    WIN $8000 $BFDF
switch    WIN bank farcall
bank      WIN 1 $81 LATHE1.BIN
bank      WIN 2 $82 LATHE2.BIN
bank      WIN 3 $83 LATHE3.BIN
bank      WIN 4 $84 LATHE4.BIN
bank      WIN 5 $85 LATHE5.BIN
unless    RAM32 bank WIN 32 $0C            ; sideways slot 12: the name heap
unless    RAM32 unless ROMFORM bank WIN 33 $0D LATHE33.BIN ; sideways slot 13: err's messages (constants) and tables
unless    RAM32 when ROMFORM bank WIN 33 $0D ; the ROM form's slot 13: tables only (its texts are the module's)
unless    RAM32 bank WIN 34 $00            ; sideways slot 0: kernel's symbol and member columns
unless    RAM32 bank WIN 35 $01            ; sideways slot 1: OUT's table and DECL's import rows
unless    RAM32 place expr WIN 1
unless    RAM32 place parts WIN 1
unless    RAM32 when ROMFORM place out WIN 1
unless    RAM32 unless ROMFORM place out WIN 4  ; bank 1 would be 226 bytes over with the variables (above)
unless    RAM32 place gen WIN 2
unless    RAM32 place lathec WIN 2
unless    RAM32 place decl WIN 3
unless    RAM32 place asmblock WIN 3
unless    RAM32 place inlines WIN 4
unless    RAM32 place kernel WIN 4
unless    RAM32 place lex WIN 4
unless    RAM32 place fbuf WIN 4
unless    RAM32 place src WIN 4
unless    RAM32 place err WIN 4
unless    RAM32 place reg WIN 5
unless    RAM32 place cond WIN 5
unless    RAM32 place fold WIN 5
unless    RAM32 place typetab WIN 5
unless    RAM32 when ROMFORM place bbcfs WIN 5 ; bbc.lth's file names with BBCFS 1 (nothing with BBCFS 0)
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region NAMES WIN 32           ; kernel.names
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region MSGS WIN 33            ; err's messages (none in the ROM form)
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region FUNCBUF WIN 33         ; fbuf.buffer, label_offset, label_uses
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region STRING WIN 33          ; lex.string
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region TOKENS WIN 33          ; kernel.tokens: INLINE's saved tokens
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region SYMS WIN 34            ; kernel's symbol and member columns
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region OUTTAB WIN 35          ; out.table and its fix-ups
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region WANTS WIN 35           ; decl's rows of what an import wants
; The image for every machine with sideways RAM (ADAPT 1, with ADFS 1: lathe/docs/bbc.md, "One
; image for every machine with sideways RAM"): the same regions, each `dynamic`, which rt_place
; puts in main RAM as it starts where they fit (the memory below $1F00 when PAGE is lower, what
; the link leaves free, a shadow screen's), in the order of these entries, each in the first area
; that holds it. Every table but WANTS has its capacity set as the tool starts (ROOMS 1; lathe/docs/
; bbc.md, "Capacities set at start-up", "One bank"): each begins at its most (`to`); when one does
; not fit, the last that has steps of 256 over its `want` gives up half of them, then the one
; before it, round and round, until all fit; when none has steps over its want they give up
; half of what they have, the same way, down to their least (`from`). The wants are what the
; machine with two banks had before the tables became planes (the compiler's own modules need
; them: the name heap 7,177, the symbols 475, the function buffer 3,402, a constant table 2,038),
; the symbols 512 rows. So the entries are in the order of how much a table matters when memory
; is short, the name heap first, and also about in the order of their sizes, so that they pack.
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region NAMES WIN 32 dynamic kernel.name_room from 3072 want 7680 to 16128
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region SYMS WIN 34 dynamic kernel.sym_rows rows 256 want 512 to 768
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region FUNCBUF WIN 33 dynamic fbuf.buffer_room from 1024 want 4096 to 4096
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region OUTTAB WIN 35 dynamic out.table_room from 512 want 2048 to 2048
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region WANTS WIN 35 dynamic
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region STRING WIN 33 dynamic lex.string_room from 512 want 2048 to 2048
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region TOKENS WIN 33 dynamic kernel.token_room from 768 want 1024 to 2048
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT region MSGS WIN 33 dynamic
unless    RAM32 when ADAPT placer rt_place
; The 32K Model B (RAM32 1): no sideways RAM, so every region is in main RAM, and the compiler is
; told so (FIXED_REGIONS above), so that no function stays fixed for a `with` block: all of the
; compiler's code but fold is in the banks.
when      RAM32 place expr WIN 1
when      RAM32 place parts WIN 1
when      RAM32 place out WIN 1
when      RAM32 place gen WIN 2
when      RAM32 place lathec WIN 2
when      RAM32 place err WIN 2
when      RAM32 place decl WIN 3
when      RAM32 place asmblock WIN 3
when      RAM32 place kernel WIN 4
when      RAM32 place lex WIN 4
when      RAM32 place src WIN 4
when      RAM32 place fbuf WIN 4
when      RAM32 place cond WIN 4
when      RAM32 place reg WIN 5
when      RAM32 place inlines WIN 5
when      RAM32 place typetab WIN 5
when      RAM32 when ROMFORM place bbcfs WIN 5
when      RAM32 unless ADAPT region NAMES fixed  ; kernel.names
when      RAM32 when ADAPT region NAMES fixed $1900  ; Image B: lowest in main RAM, from the DFS's PAGE
when      RAM32 region MSGS fixed            ; err's messages (none in the ROM form)
when      RAM32 region FUNCBUF fixed         ; fbuf.buffer, label_offset, label_uses
when      RAM32 region STRING fixed          ; lex.string
when      RAM32 region TOKENS fixed          ; kernel.tokens: INLINE's saved tokens
when      RAM32 region SYMS fixed            ; kernel's symbol and member columns
when      RAM32 region OUTTAB fixed          ; out.table and its fix-ups
when      RAM32 region WANTS fixed           ; decl's rows of what an import wants
farcall   rt_bbc
